		Bestiary: {
			LavaWorm: A worm that adapted to the scorching hot temperatures of the cave. It burrows through the hot magma, inflicting the same burns it first recieved on anyone who touches it.
			RhyoliteSlimer: A slime that seems to be made out of still forming Rhyolite, with the gel inside holding the rock together.
			Bandit: Seemingly a bandit that arrived to ransack this abandoned land. Even if they aren't durable, the dagger's they seem too possess often are still extremely deadly.
			BanditLooter: A knife-throwing Bandit. He seems to have looted more goodies than a typical Bandit. Probably still alive because of the knives however, so don't get hit!
			CrimsonCultist: A cultist that will sacrifice living beings to make sure The Crimson grows. Bandits, townsfolk, doesn't matter who, they will sacrifice you too. Sometimes in a desperate situation, they may even sacrifice themselves to it!
			HauntedArmor: Left behind, presumably by its owner, this abandoned armor became haunted to seek revenge on them... However since it can't see, it probably assumes any human is its owner.
			SporeSlime: Despite spores being in it, it doesn't appear to be dying... Infact, the slime and spores seem to have a symbiotic relationship. It seems like the Glowing Snail are its source of food
			NightmareWalker: A person devoid of life. They are lost souls turned evil by the Corruption, now seemingly a walking nightmare. Reminder that the original person can see everything that happens but are helpless to stop it...
			SnowLeopard: A solitary predator that seeks its prey in the tundra. It rarely hunts humans...
			Wartornmelon: Cut enemy for now
			TempleSentry: A dangerous sentry that patrols the Lihzahrd Temple, shooting lasers and ramming into those who run into the temple uninvited. Low grade weapons won't even scratch it without the help of souls being released...
			HalfDigested: An unfortunate bipedal mortal like a human or goblin, ate and spat out by the Stomach Of Cthulhu. They now run about to harm those not yet under this affliction.
			StomachBug: A small stinkbug now turned into a denizen of the Corrosion. Stomach Bugs run about gathering food for the ever hungry overlord, all the while covering the land in their noxious fumes.
			Gastritis: Annoying, plentiful, ugly, reckless, and deadly. That's what Gastritis are, and that's bad news for you.
			Evphila: These cockroaches adapted to the environment over quite a few centuries. Born into a vile and evil world, they feed off the sins of their surroundings. Thankfully, they can't fly.
			Capillarie: Aggressive crimified worms that tunnel fast. They are extremely small and frail; however, they compensate with their surprising lethality.
			TapeWorm: A class of parasitic worms that have adapted to go unnoticed by the Corrosion. other than that, they are quite weak however they can withstand plenty.
			CorruptCultist: An unfortunate soul whose intent turned evil. They may be one of the most sadistic beings out there.
			CorrodedCultist: No one knows why they worship what's essentially a digestive evil, however they're as deadly as any other mysterious cult member.
			Tiger: A predator native to the jungle that sneaks up on its prey and pounces on it until its dead.
			MarbleElemental: Earth elementals manifest through many forms by taking on the properties of different materials, such as this sturdy marble.
			OnyxPenguin: The Onyx Penguins are a oddity. Onyx gemstones only come from the area where even lava becomes frozen. so how did these penguins get here?
		}

